cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Theoretical Foundations of Neural Networks and PINNs for
  Differential Equations
message: "If you use this software or the accompanying thesis, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Nguyễn
    given-names: Hoàng Tú
abstract: >-
  A from-scratch PyTorch implementation of physics-informed neural networks,
  written to test the theory it accompanies rather than to wrap an existing
  library. Six experiments probe the failure modes the thesis predicts: the
  degeneracy of ReLU under a second-order operator, the finite optimal penalty
  weight of a soft boundary constraint, operator-induced reversal of spectral
  bias, and a numerical certificate for the stability bound
  ‖e‖ ≤ π⁻²‖r‖ — together with the hypothesis under which it fails.
keywords:
  - physics-informed neural networks
  - scientific machine learning
  - partial differential equations
  - automatic differentiation
  - spectral bias
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-05"
